vo_mediacodec: request the isolated event-prefetch renderer

The event pre-render asks sd_ass for its isolated prefetch state (patch
0013) with OSD_DRAW_PREFETCH, and the vo.rst description of the OSD plane
says what that buys. Split from 0013 so the sub/ half can be shared with
the other VOs that pre-render subtitles.

diff --git a/DOCS/man/vo.rst b/DOCS/man/vo.rst
index e1bf520..e1d8eb6 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/vo.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/vo.rst
@@ -752,10 +752,17 @@ Available video output drivers are:
     known to the VO, pre-rendered for the next frame from the observed frame
     cadence while the current one waits for its deadline, and, while the OSD
     is static, for the first frame of the next subtitle event ahead of its
-    start (never past what the subtitle decoders have read). Event pre-renders
-    warm the renderer and GPU caches but are not presented directly: each
-    request uses a timestamp-matched render, reusing the prepared atlas when
-    the pixels match. A render that repeats the pixels already on screen is
+    start (never past what the subtitle decoders have read). ASS event
+    pre-renders retain a separate renderer and packed atlas, so intervening
+    current-frame renders cannot evict their prepared state. At handoff only
+    the old renderer's event-layout snapshots are released; both renderers,
+    their raster/font caches and worker pools remain reusable. The exact
+    requested timestamp is rendered, including repeated requests at the same
+    timestamp: an unchanged result reuses the prepared atlas, not an image
+    accepted by age. Reset, option changes and output deselection discard the
+    pending renderer. This prefetch path is used by this Android VO; it does
+    not enable persistent libass layout caching.
+    A render that repeats the pixels already on screen is
     folded into them and costs no swap. Rasterized frames are
     uploaded and composed on the GPU while the present thread is idle, and
     presented through a GLES2 surface over the OSD Surface with the same
